# reco-now's own domain, as terms — owned by this app (ext-apps/Reco/),
# never by graph-owl's packs/ directory.
#
# Every term here is a *runtime* term: the namespace is allocated by
# POST /namespaces and each predicate registered by POST /predicates, so
# nothing here required a line of Rust — the same claim
# plans/105-domain-neutrality.md makes checkable for packs/gst and
# packs/hospitality, now checked a third time by a pack this repository
# did not author.
#
# Field set and labels are reco-now's own (ext-apps/Reco/backend/app/
# main.py's FIELD_LABELS) — not copied from packs/gst/ontology.ttl, whose
# invoice model has no HSN code, IMS status, note type, voucher fields or
# original-invoice-number.

@prefix reco: <https://reconow.dev/pack#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# **Two classes, matching reco-now's own `kind` values** (main.py's
# dataset "books"/"gstr2b") rather than inventing new vocabulary for a
# distinction the app already draws. A books row and a portal row for the
# same real invoice are two separate subjects here, same as
# gst:PurchaseInvoice/gst:Gstr2bInvoice keep separate per-source evidence
# — Slice 2's reconciliation is what relates them, not this ontology.
reco:BooksInvoice  rdf:type reco:Class ; reco:label "Purchase register entry (your books)" .
reco:PortalInvoice rdf:type reco:Class ; reco:label "GSTR-2B entry (government data)" .

reco:invoiceNumber rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Invoice Number" .
reco:supplierGstin rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Supplier GSTIN" .
reco:supplierName  rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Supplier Name" .
reco:taxableValue  rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Taxable Amount" .
reco:invoiceDate   rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Invoice Date" .
reco:placeOfSupply rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Place of Supply" .
reco:hsnCode       rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "HSN Code" .
reco:imsStatus     rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "IMS Status" .
reco:reverseCharge rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Reverse Charge" .
reco:noteType      rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Note Type" .
reco:voucherType   rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Voucher Type" .

# Debit/credit-note fields — a note references the invoice it corrects,
# by number, as the source data carries it. Not modelled as a graph edge
# in Slice 1: the referenced invoice may not be in the same upload, and a
# dangling `reco:Ref` would be a broken edge rather than a missing fact.
reco:originalInvoiceNumber rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Original Invoice No" .
reco:voucherNumber         rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Voucher No" .

# The four tax components the authority reports separately. reco-now's
# own reconciliation.py already sums these as `record_tax`; kept as
# separate facts here for the same reason packs/gst keeps them separate —
# an intra-/inter-state mismatch the total alone would hide.
reco:igst rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "IGST" .
reco:cgst rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "CGST" .
reco:sgst rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "SGST" .
reco:cess rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Cess" .
